### The two `onDelete` policies the descriptor declares, measured against each other. This case runs
### last on purpose: it destroys the rows the earlier ones built.
###
### State it inherits: Ada holds task `a`; Grace holds `b` and `d`; Zoe holds nothing. Tasks `a` and
### `c` are on milestone Beta, `d` is on Launch, `e` is on neither.
###
### Deleting Ada is refused — `tasks.assignee_id` is `restrict`, so a person who still holds work
### cannot be removed. The alternative would be silently unassigning her tasks, which loses the one
### fact somebody would have wanted to look up.
# @name DeleteAdaRefused
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [409]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/people/{{AdaId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}

### Zoe holds nothing, and goes. The control: without it, the 409 above could be "delete is broken"
### rather than "the reference stopped it".
# @name DeleteZoe
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [204]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/people/{{ZoeId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}

### Beta goes, and `tasks.milestone_id` is `cascade`, so the tasks on it go with it. A task belonging
### to a milestone that no longer exists is orphaned data, not history.
# @name DeleteBeta
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [204]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/milestones/{{BetaId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}

### What is left of this run's tasks
# @name TasksAfterCascade
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?title=like.{{runToken}}%25&order=title.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}

### Ada now holds nothing — the cascade took the task that was blocking her — so the same delete that
### was refused above succeeds. The restrict was about the reference, and it lifted with it.
# @name DeleteAdaNow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [204]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/people/{{AdaId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}

### And the team is Grace alone
# @name TeamAfter
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/people?name=like.{{runToken}}%25&order=name.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}
